coi selpa'i

I was puzzled by the use of logic connectives in several passages. E.g.

(1) {z=E0sti fa no sai dr=F9sro je no lolnitk=F9'a}
(2) {no tr=ECcu je no zd=E0ni cu zv=E0ti}

I see there is some consistency in their correlation with quantifiers, but
still I don't get it. What is the logic behind them?

They are rejected by both camxes and jboski, but accepted by the parser you
indicated. Nevertheless, the parser also understands {ko'a je ko'e broda}
just like {ko'a .e ko'e broda}. Is it related to expansion order?

mu'o mi'e .asiz.

